# Risk Domain

Consequences of failure determine how careful the AI should be. Internal dashboards tolerate bugs unacceptable in payment processing.

## Options

RiskLevels {
  Personal => Inconvenience to author only
  Internal => Affects colleagues, wastes time
  Business => Affects customers, revenue, reputation
  Financial => Money lost, regulatory issues, lawsuits
  Healthcare => Patient harm, regulatory penalties
  Security => Enables attacks, data breaches
}

## AI Behavior Calibration

BehaviorsByRisk {
  Personal => skip security push, trust inputs, simple errors, relaxed about local creds
  Internal => basic auth, validate to prevent mistakes, clear errors, don't over-engineer
  Business => enforce auth, validate external input, sanitize output, structured logging, flag privacy
  Financial => insist on security, validate everything, audit logging, idempotency, flag secrets
  Healthcare => strict access control, encryption, audit trail, fail-safe, flag PII/PHI
  Security => assume hostile input, whitelist validation, constant-time secrets, minimal error info
}

## Risk × Lifecycle

| | PoC | MVP | Production |
|---|-----|-----|------------|
| Personal | Skip | Basic | Standard |
| Internal | Basic auth | + validation | + logging |
| Business | Auth skeleton | Full auth | + audit |
| Financial | Security basics | Full security | Defense in depth |
| Healthcare | Compliance skeleton | + audit | Full compliance |
| Security | Security-first | Full security | Paranoid |

Constraints {
  Even PoC for financial/healthcare needs security basics.
  Risk level overrides lifecycle for security concerns.
}
